@vsoch The point and question is regarding the Library API, there is no OCI registry that implements that protocol which is why Paul asked if there will be a publicly available implementation of it.

If not, we will probably have to use the Sylabs implementation, or remove the CI testing.

My feeling is we should be testing the Library API, and if there is no non-commercial endpoint for it, then we should use the commercial endpoint, and hope that we don't get ourselves blocked or rate limited (which has much precedent at this point).

