body:
I'm not sure of all the side effects of this.  I think it would be safer to only add to do this when buildArgs.encrypt is set in a non-suid situation, that is
```
if os.Getuid() != 0 {
        if isDeffile {
                sylog.Verbosef("Implying --fakeroot because building from Deffile file unprivileged")
                fakerootExec(true)
        } else if buildArgs.encrypt && (buildcfg.APPTAINER_SUID_INSTALL == 0 || buildArgs.userns) {
                sylog.Verbosef("Implying --fakeroot because using unprivileged encryption")
                fakerootExec(true)
        }
```
Then inside `fakerootExec()` change the name of the bool parameter to `required` and change the message when it is false to
```
        sylog.Fatalf("Building from a definition file or using encryption unprivileged requires either a suid installation or unprivileged user namespaces")
````

