body:
instead of passing it to the container environment, you could directly use it to generate the context timeout here with:

```
// runscript-timeout is set, parse the duration and return an error if any,
// otherwise the timeout is set to 1 minute by default.
var execCtx context.Context
if timeoutVal := engineConfig.GetRunscriptTimeout(); timeoutVal != "" {
    timeoutDur, err := time.ParseDuration(timeoutVal)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, nil, err
    }
    execCtx = context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), timeoutDur.Abs())
} else {
    execCtx = context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), time.Minute)
}
```

then replace all `context.TODO()` in `runActionScript` by `execCtx`

